# dotfiles-Offense/.gitignore
# =============================================================================
# This is a PUBLIC showcase repo. Engagement data must NEVER land here.
# Primary defense: all engagement data lives in ~/engagements (outside the repo).
# This file is defense-in-depth in case anything ever gets copied in by mistake.
# =============================================================================

# NOTE ON SYNTAX: git only treats `#` as a comment at the START of a line. An
# inline "pattern   # why" comment makes the WHOLE line the pattern, so it matches
# nothing — a silently dead rule. Every comment below is therefore on its own line.

# ── engagement / client data — hard block ────────────────────────────────────
# These are the directory names `mkengagement` actually creates (see
# offensive/offensive.zsh and offensive/templates/engagement.md). Keep all three
# in step: a name that drifts in one is a name this backstop stops covering.
engagements/
scope/
recon/
scans/
nmap/
web/
loot/
creds/
hashes/
bloodhound/
screenshots/
exploit/
report/
notes/
notes.md
scope.txt
scope.md
*.scope
# Retired names, kept so an OLD engagement tree copied in is still covered.
evidence/
exploits/

# ── captures, hashes, cred stores, scanner output ────────────────────────────
*.pcap
*.cap
*.hccapx
*.kdbx
*.ntds
*.dit
hashes*
*.nessus
*.gnmap
*.nmap
# nmap/burp/scanner exports — review before ever un-ignoring.
*.xml
# BloodHound/SharpHound collector bundles, and archives generally: the CE-ready
# zip `bhce` produces is loot, and no archive belongs in this repo.
*.zip
secrets*
*.creds
# Kerberos + cracking artifacts.
*.kirbi
*.ccache
*.potfile
*.restore

# ── secrets / env ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
# Keystores / client certs / VPN + RDP profiles — each one carries a credential.
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
*.ovpn
*.rdp

# ── ssh: nothing tracked ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The sanitized ssh/config moved to dotfiles-Debian with the OS-native layer. The
# ignore stays: keys and per-host configs must never land here by accident, and this
# repo has no reason to track anything under ssh/ any more.
ssh/*

# ── local-only / generated ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# v4 renamed the host-local override fragment; the pre-v4 name is kept so a box
# mid-migration is still covered.
zsh/99-local.zsh
zsh/local.zsh
.claude/settings.local.json
*.pre-dotfiles.*
*.log
*.bak

# ── OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
__pycache__/
*.pyc
